# webOS Remote Key Event Handlers & Shelf Auto-Scroll Architecture Specification

**Module**: `app/js/navigation.js` (`window.SpatialNav`) & `app/js/app.js` (`window.CinejoyApp`)  
**Milestone**: Milestone 3 (Deterministic Spatial Remote Navigation Engine)  
**Target Environment**: LG webOS 8.5.0 (Chromium ~108+), LG 32LR686BPSA Television (1920×1080 Full HD Canvas)  
**Author**: `explorer_m3_2_gen2`  
**Status**: Ready for Implementation by `worker_m3`  
**Companion Documents**: 
- `spatial_algorithm_spec.md` (`explorer_m3_1_gen2`)
- `test_m3_spec.md` (`explorer_m3_3_gen2`)

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Architectural Scope

In a 10-foot television user experience, touchscreens and mouse pointers do not exist. All user interactions are conducted via the LG webOS Magic Remote or infrared (IR) remote control from a distance of 8 to 12 feet.

This document establishes the technical architecture and implementation specification for:
1. **webOS Remote Keycode Map & Dispatcher**: Full normalization and deterministic handling of D-pad arrows (38, 40, 37, 39), Enter/OK (13), the webOS Back button (keycode 461 / 27), Media control keys (Play 415/179, Pause 19, Stop 413/178, FastForward 417/228, Rewind 412/227), and dedicated Color keys (Red 403, Green 404, Yellow 405, Blue 406).
2. **Two-Tier Viewport & Shelf Auto-Scrolling**: A high-performance auto-scrolling subsystem that keeps active UI components strictly within SMPTE RP 2046-1 5% TV-safe margins (96px horizontal padding, 54px vertical padding), guarantees visibility of content shelf headers beneath the 84px fixed glass application header, and eliminates visual clipping.
3. **Integration Contract**: Seamless interoperability between `SpatialNav`, `CinejoyApp`, the on-screen TV virtual keyboard in `#view-search`, and fullscreen playback controls in `#view-player`.

```
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                LG webOS 8.5 Remote Control Event Flow                             |
|                                                                                                   |
|    [ D-Pad Arrows ]     [ OK / Enter (13) ]    [ Back (461 / 27) ]   [ Media / Color Keys ]        |
|    (38, 40, 37, 39)              |                      |                      |                  |
|           |                      |                      |                      |                  |
|           v                      v                      v                      v                  |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+  |
|  |                             SpatialNav.handleKeyDown(event)                                 |  |
|  |    - Normalize keycode / key string                                                         |  |
|  |    - Key-repeat rate limiter (60ms throttle on D-pad)                                       |  |
|  |    - event.preventDefault() on recognized keys                                              |  |
|  +--------+----------------------+----------------------+----------------------+---------------+  |
|           |                      |                      |                      |                  |
|           v                      v                      v                      v                  |
|    [ SpatialNav.move ]     [ Element Click ]    [ Hierarchical Back ]   [ Event Bus Emit ]        |
|           |                      |                      |                      |                  |
|           v                      |                      v                      v                  |
|  +-----------------------+       |             +-----------------+    +-----------------+         |
|  |  SpatialNav.setFocus  |       |             | CinejoyApp      |    | Player OSD /    |         |
|  +--------+--------------+       |             | handleBack()    |    | Search Keyboard |         |
|           |                      |             +-----------------+    +-----------------+         |
|           v                      |                                                                |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+  |
|  |                          Two-Tier TV-Safe Auto-Scroll Subsystem                             |  |
|  |                                                                                             |  |
|  |  Tier 1: Horizontal Shelf Auto-Scroll (.shelf-rail)                                         |  |
|  |    - Offsets active card relative to 96px left / right TV-safe margins                       |  |
|  |    - Peek preview offset (48px) for upcoming off-screen cards                              |  |
|  |                                                                                             |  |
|  |  Tier 2: Vertical Viewport Auto-Scroll (.view-scroll-pane)                                  |  |
|  |    - Header clearance offset (84px fixed header + 20px buffer = 104px top boundary)         |  |
|  |    - Bottom boundary clearance (1080px - 54px = 1026px bottom boundary)                     |  |
|  |    - Shelf section title retention (aligns .content-shelf header into view)                 |  |
|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

---

## 2. webOS Remote Keycodes & Event Dispatcher Architecture

### 2.1 Complete webOS Remote Keycode Reference Table

webOS Chromium (~108+) exposes remote control actions through standard DOM `KeyboardEvent` objects. Due to variations between LG Magic Remotes (RF pointer + wheel click), standard IR replacement remotes, and desktop browser emulation, `SpatialNav` must accept both modern `event.key` strings and traditional `event.keyCode` integers.

| Semantic Action | webOS `keyCode` | Desktop / Fallback `keyCode` | `event.key` Values | Target Behavior |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `MOVE_UP` | `38` | `38` | `'ArrowUp'`, `'Up'` | Move focus upward |
| `MOVE_DOWN` | `40` | `40` | `'ArrowDown'`, `'Down'` | Move focus downward |
| `MOVE_LEFT` | `37` | `37` | `'ArrowLeft'`, `'Left'` | Move focus leftward |
| `MOVE_RIGHT` | `39` | `39` | `'ArrowRight'`, `'Right'` | Move focus rightward |
| `SELECT` | `13` | `13` | `'Enter'` | Trigger `click()` on active element |
| `BACK` | `461` | `27` | `'Back'`, `'XF86Back'`, `'GoBack'`, `'Escape'` | Hierarchical backward navigation |
| `BACKSPACE` | `8` | `8` | `'Backspace'` | Delete character in search input |
| `MEDIA_PLAY` | `415` | `179` | `'MediaPlay'`, `'Play'` | Play active media |
| `MEDIA_PAUSE` | `19` | `19` | `'MediaPause'`, `'Pause'` | Pause active media |
| `MEDIA_PLAY_PAUSE` | `179` | `179` | `'MediaPlayPause'` | Toggle play/pause |
| `MEDIA_STOP` | `413` | `178` | `'MediaStop'`, `'Stop'` | Stop playback & exit to details |
| `MEDIA_FAST_FORWARD`| `417` | `228` | `'MediaFastForward'`, `'FastForward'` | Seek +10s in stream |
| `MEDIA_REWIND` | `412` | `227` | `'MediaRewind'`, `'Rewind'` | Seek -10s in stream |
| `COLOR_RED` | `403` | N/A | `'ColorF0Red'`, `'Red'` | Context action 1 (Search / Clear) |
| `COLOR_GREEN` | `404` | N/A | `'ColorF1Green'`, `'Green'` | Context action 2 (Movies / Space) |
| `COLOR_YELLOW` | `405` | N/A | `'ColorF2Yellow'`, `'Yellow'` | Context action 3 (Series Hub) |
| `COLOR_BLUE` | `406` | N/A | `'ColorF3Blue'`, `'Blue'` | Context action 4 (Home View) |
| `NUM_0` - `NUM_9` | `48` - `57` | `48` - `57` | `'0'` - `'9'` | Direct numeric entry |

### 2.2 Keycode Constants Dictionary (`SpatialNav.KEY_CODES`)

```javascript
SpatialNav.KEY_CODES = Object.freeze({
  // Directional D-Pad
  UP: [38],
  DOWN: [40],
  LEFT: [37],
  RIGHT: [39],

  // Confirmation
  ENTER: [13],

  // Back Navigation (461: webOS Remote, 27: Escape fallback)
  BACK: [461, 27],
  BACKSPACE: [8],

  // Media Playback Controls
  PLAY: [415, 179],
  PAUSE: [19],
  PLAY_PAUSE: [179],
  STOP: [413, 178],
  FAST_FORWARD: [417, 228],
  REWIND: [412, 227],

  // webOS Dedicated Color Keys
  COLOR_RED: [403],
  COLOR_GREEN: [404],
  COLOR_YELLOW: [405],
  COLOR_BLUE: [406]
});
```

### 2.3 Event Normalization & Action Resolver

The helper function `resolveKeyAction(event)` translates heterogeneous `KeyboardEvent` properties into unified semantic action tokens:

```javascript
function resolveKeyAction(e) {
  var code = e.keyCode || e.which;
  var key = e.key || '';

  // 1. D-Pad Navigation
  if (code === 38 || key === 'ArrowUp' || key === 'Up') return 'MOVE_UP';
  if (code === 40 || key === 'ArrowDown' || key === 'Down') return 'MOVE_DOWN';
  if (code === 37 || key === 'ArrowLeft' || key === 'Left') return 'MOVE_LEFT';
  if (code === 39 || key === 'ArrowRight' || key === 'Right') return 'MOVE_RIGHT';

  // 2. Select / Confirmation
  if (code === 13 || key === 'Enter') return 'SELECT';

  // 3. Back Navigation
  if (code === 461 || code === 27 || key === 'Escape' || key === 'Back' || key === 'XF86Back') {
    return 'BACK';
  }
  if (code === 8 || key === 'Backspace') return 'BACKSPACE';

  // 4. Media Playback
  if (code === 415 || (code === 179 && key === 'MediaPlay') || key === 'Play') return 'MEDIA_PLAY';
  if (code === 19 || key === 'MediaPause' || key === 'Pause') return 'MEDIA_PAUSE';
  if (code === 179 || key === 'MediaPlayPause') return 'MEDIA_PLAY_PAUSE';
  if (code === 413 || code === 178 || key === 'MediaStop' || key === 'Stop') return 'MEDIA_STOP';
  if (code === 417 || code === 228 || key === 'MediaFastForward' || key === 'FastForward') return 'MEDIA_FAST_FORWARD';
  if (code === 412 || code === 227 || key === 'MediaRewind' || key === 'Rewind') return 'MEDIA_REWIND';

  // 5. webOS Color Buttons
  if (code === 403 || key === 'ColorF0Red' || key === 'Red') return 'COLOR_RED';
  if (code === 404 || key === 'ColorF1Green' || key === 'Green') return 'COLOR_GREEN';
  if (code === 405 || key === 'ColorF2Yellow' || key === 'Yellow') return 'COLOR_YELLOW';
  if (code === 406 || key === 'ColorF3Blue' || key === 'Blue') return 'COLOR_BLUE';

  return null;
}
```

### 2.4 D-Pad Key Repeat Throttling Mechanism

#### The webOS Repeat Problem:
When an end-user holds down a directional key on an LG remote control, the hardware remote continuously sends pulse signals. webOS fires `keydown` events at approximately **120ms to 150ms** intervals. If spatial vector calculations, bounding rect measurements, and smooth scroll operations are initiated synchronously on every tick without throttling:
1. The DOM layout engine suffers from layout thrashing and dropped animation frames.
2. The smooth-scroll animation queue builds up lag, causing the shelf to continue scrolling long after the user has released the button.

#### The Solution:
`SpatialNav` incorporates a 60ms minimum time gate between successive directional movements. If a directional keydown occurs within 60ms of the previous movement, it is discarded. If key events arrive faster than 100ms for more than 3 consecutive ticks (indicating continuous hold), `SpatialNav` switches smooth scrolling from `'smooth'` to `'auto'` (instant) to keep visual focus locked synchronously with the remote:

```javascript
var throttleState = {
  lastMoveTimestamp: 0,
  minIntervalMs: 60,
  rapidCount: 0
};

function shouldThrottleMovement() {
  var now = Date.now();
  var delta = now - throttleState.lastMoveTimestamp;
  if (delta < throttleState.minIntervalMs) {
    return true; // Drop event
  }
  if (delta < 120) {
    throttleState.rapidCount++;
  } else {
    throttleState.rapidCount = 0;
  }
  throttleState.lastMoveTimestamp = now;
  return false;
}
```

### 2.5 Central Keydown Dispatcher Specification (`SpatialNav.handleKeyDown`)

```javascript
SpatialNav.handleKeyDown = function (event) {
  if (!this.isEnabled()) return;
  if (!event) return;

  var action = resolveKeyAction(event);
  if (!action) return;

  // 1. Directional Movements
  if (action === 'MOVE_UP' || action === 'MOVE_DOWN' || action === 'MOVE_LEFT' || action === 'MOVE_RIGHT') {
    if (shouldThrottleMovement()) {
      event.preventDefault();
      return;
    }
    event.preventDefault();
    var directionMap = {
      'MOVE_UP': 'up',
      'MOVE_DOWN': 'down',
      'MOVE_LEFT': 'left',
      'MOVE_RIGHT': 'right'
    };
    var dir = directionMap[action];
    var movedElement = this.move(dir, event);
    if (!movedElement) {
      this.emit('deadend', { direction: dir, current: this.getCurrentFocus() });
    }
    return;
  }

  // 2. Select / Confirmation (Enter/OK key)
  if (action === 'SELECT') {
    event.preventDefault();
    var current = this.getCurrentFocus();
    if (current) {
      this.emit('select', { element: current });
      // Standard dispatch: execute click on interactive element
      current.click();
    }
    return;
  }

  // 3. webOS Back Navigation (Keycode 461 / 27)
  if (action === 'BACK') {
    event.preventDefault();
    this.handleBackNavigation();
    return;
  }

  // 4. Media Playback Controls
  if (action.indexOf('MEDIA_') === 0) {
    event.preventDefault();
    this.emit('mediakey', {
      action: action,
      keyCode: event.keyCode || event.which,
      originalEvent: event
    });
    return;
  }

  // 5. Dedicated Color Keys
  if (action.indexOf('COLOR_') === 0) {
    event.preventDefault();
    this.emit('colorkey', {
      color: action.replace('COLOR_', '').toLowerCase(),
      keyCode: event.keyCode || event.which,
      originalEvent: event
    });
    return;
  }
};
```

