## 3. Viewport & Shelf Auto-Scrolling Architecture

### 3.1 Two-Tier Auto-Scroll Hierarchy

The Cinejoy application layout contains two distinct, nested scrollable containers:

```
[ .views-container (1920x1080 fixed window) ]
  └── #view-{currentView} (1920x1080)
        └── .view-scroll-pane  <--- TIER 2: Vertical Viewport Scroll Container
              ├── .app-header (Fixed 84px glass bar, z-index 100)
              ├── .hero-banner (600px height)
              └── .content-shelf
                    ├── .shelf-header (Shelf title "Trending Movies")
                    └── .shelf-rail  <--- TIER 1: Horizontal Shelf Rail Container
                          ├── .card-poster (Card 1: 220px)
                          ├── .card-poster (Card 2: 220px)
                          └── ...
```

1. **Tier 1 (Horizontal Shelf Rail - `.shelf-rail`)**:
   - Manages horizontal movement across carousel cards.
   - Adjusts container `scrollLeft`.
   - Leaves vertical scrolling unaffected.
2. **Tier 2 (Vertical Viewport - `.view-scroll-pane`)**:
   - Manages vertical page navigation between the hero banner, content shelves, and grid rows.
   - Adjusts container `scrollTop`.
   - Prevents elements from scrolling under the 84px fixed header.

### 3.2 5% TV-Safe Area Geometry & Constants

In accordance with SMPTE RP 2046-1 and EBU R95 standards, 10-foot television layouts require a minimum 5% title-safe margin on all edges:

$$\text{SafeMarginX} = 1920 \times 0.05 = 96\text{px}$$
$$\text{SafeMarginY} = 1080 \times 0.05 = 54\text{px}$$
$$\text{UsableWidth} = 1920 - (2 \times 96) = 1728\text{px}$$
$$\text{UsableHeight} = 1080 - (2 \times 54) = 972\text{px}$$

| Boundary Parameter | Value | Definition & Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `SAFE_X_MIN` | `96px` | Left TV-safe boundary. Elements must not extend left of this coordinate. |
| `SAFE_X_MAX` | `1824px` | Right TV-safe boundary ($1920 - 96$). Elements must not extend right of this coordinate. |
| `SAFE_Y_MIN` | `54px` | Raw top TV-safe boundary ($1080 \times 0.05$). |
| `HEADER_HEIGHT`| `84px` | Height of the fixed glass `.app-header`. |
| `EFFECTIVE_Y_MIN` | `104px` | Effective top boundary below fixed header ($84\text{px} + 20\text{px}$ buffer). |
| `SAFE_Y_MAX` | `1026px` | Bottom TV-safe boundary ($1080 - 54$). Elements must not extend below this coordinate. |
| `PEEK_OFFSET` | `48px` | Horizontal visual anticipation buffer revealing the edge of the next off-screen card. |

---

### 3.3 Horizontal Shelf Auto-Scroll Algorithm (`.shelf-rail`)

#### Mathematical Formulation:
Let the scroll container $C$ be the `.shelf-rail` element.
Let the newly focused element be $E$ (e.g. `.card-poster`, `.card-provider`, `.card-episode`).
Let $E_{\text{rect}} = E.\text{getBoundingClientRect}()$.
Let $C_{\text{rect}} = C.\text{getBoundingClientRect}()$.

The horizontal position of $E$ relative to the 1920px screen is given by:
$$E_{\text{left}} = E_{\text{rect}}.\text{left}, \quad E_{\text{right}} = E_{\text{rect}}.\text{right}$$

#### Execution Logic:
1. **Case 1: First Element in Shelf (Index 0 or leftmost edge)**:
   If $E$ is the first navigable child in $C$ or $E.\text{offsetLeft} \le 96\text{px}$:
   $$\text{targetScrollLeft} = 0$$
   *Rationale*: Snaps the shelf cleanly back to the left margin without fractional offset drift.

2. **Case 2: Element Clipped on Left ($E_{\text{left}} < 96\text{px}$)**:
   The user has navigated backward to the left. The element is partially or completely cut off by the left safe boundary:
   $$\Delta_{\text{left}} = 96 - E_{\text{left}}$$
   $$\text{targetScrollLeft} = \max\left(0, C.\text{scrollLeft} - \Delta_{\text{left}}\right)$$
   *Rationale*: Brings the card into the visible safe zone with exactly 96px left margin.

3. **Case 3: Element Clipped on Right ($E_{\text{right}} > 1824\text{px}$)**:
   The user has navigated forward to the right. The element extends past the 1824px right safe boundary:
   $$\Delta_{\text{right}} = E_{\text{right}} - 1824$$
   $$\text{targetScrollLeft} = C.\text{scrollLeft} + \Delta_{\text{right}} + \text{PEEK\_OFFSET}$$
   Where $\text{PEEK\_OFFSET} = 48\text{px}$.
   *Rationale*: Shifts the rail so the focused card is entirely within the safe area, plus an extra 48px to reveal the leading edge of the subsequent card. This creates visual affordance that more content exists on the shelf.

4. **Case 4: Element Already Fully Inside $[96\text{px}, 1824\text{px}]$**:
   If $E_{\text{left}} \ge 96\text{px}$ and $E_{\text{right}} \le 1824\text{px}$:
   No horizontal scroll operation is performed.
   *Rationale*: Prevents unnecessary scroll events when traversing cards already in full view.

#### Implementation Specification:
```javascript
SpatialNav.autoScrollShelf = function (element) {
  if (!element) return;

  var rail = element.closest('.shelf-rail, .cards-carousel, [data-scroll-rail="true"]');
  if (!rail) return;

  var SAFE_X_MIN = 96;
  var SAFE_X_MAX = 1824; // 1920 - 96
  var PEEK_OFFSET = 48;

  // Case 1: First element reset
  if (!element.previousElementSibling || element.getAttribute('data-nav-index') === '0') {
    if (rail.scrollLeft !== 0) {
      rail.scrollTo({ left: 0, behavior: throttleState.rapidCount > 2 ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
    }
    return;
  }

  var rect = element.getBoundingClientRect();
  var currentScroll = rail.scrollLeft;

  // Case 2: Clipped on Left
  if (rect.left < SAFE_X_MIN) {
    var deltaLeft = SAFE_X_MIN - rect.left;
    var targetLeft = Math.max(0, currentScroll - deltaLeft);
    rail.scrollTo({ left: targetLeft, behavior: throttleState.rapidCount > 2 ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
    return;
  }

  // Case 3: Clipped on Right
  if (rect.right > SAFE_X_MAX) {
    var deltaRight = rect.right - SAFE_X_MAX;
    var maxScroll = rail.scrollWidth - rail.clientWidth;
    var targetRight = Math.min(maxScroll, currentScroll + deltaRight + PEEK_OFFSET);
    rail.scrollTo({ left: targetRight, behavior: throttleState.rapidCount > 2 ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
    return;
  }
};
```

---

### 3.4 Vertical Viewport Auto-Scroll Algorithm (`.view-scroll-pane`)

#### Mathematical Formulation:
Let scroll container $V$ be the `.view-scroll-pane` element of the active view.
Let element $E$ be the newly focused item.
Let $E_{\text{top}} = E.\text{getBoundingClientRect}().\text{top}$.
Let $E_{\text{bottom}} = E.\text{getBoundingClientRect}().\text{bottom}$.

Effective boundaries:
- Top boundary ($M_{\text{top}}$): $104\text{px}$ ($84\text{px}$ header height $+ 20\text{px}$ breathing room).
- Bottom boundary ($M_{\text{bottom}}$): $1026\text{px}$ ($1080\text{px} - 54\text{px}$).

#### Execution Logic:
1. **Case 1: Element is inside Header (`.app-header`)**:
   When focus moves to a header pill (`.nav-pill-item` or `.brand-container`), the viewport must reset to top:
   $$\text{targetScrollTop} = 0$$

2. **Case 2: Element is inside Hero Banner (`.hero-banner`)**:
   When focus is within the hero banner buttons (`#hero-play-btn`, `#hero-details-btn`):
   $$\text{targetScrollTop} = 0$$

3. **Case 3: Element belongs to a Content Shelf (`.content-shelf`)**:
   A content shelf consists of a section header (`.shelf-header` with title "Trending Movies") and the cards rail (`.shelf-rail`). If we only scroll until the focused card is visible, the shelf header is frequently pushed behind the fixed header, disorienting the viewer.
   Let $S = E.\text{closest}('.content-shelf')$.
   Let $S_{\text{top}} = S.\text{getBoundingClientRect}().\text{top}$.
   Let $S_{\text{bottom}} = S.\text{getBoundingClientRect}().\text{bottom}$.

   - **Sub-case 3a (Shelf top occluded by header, $S_{\text{top}} < M_{\text{top}}$)**:
     Scroll $V$ upward until the entire shelf header is revealed at $M_{\text{top}}$:
     $$\Delta_{\text{top}} = M_{\text{top}} - S_{\text{top}}$$
     $$\text{targetScrollTop} = \max\left(0, V.\text{scrollTop} - \Delta_{\text{top}}\right)$$

   - **Sub-case 3b (Card bottom clipped by bottom safe area, $E_{\text{bottom}} > M_{\text{bottom}}$)**:
     Scroll $V$ downward so the card and its rating badge are comfortably within the safe area:
     $$\Delta_{\text{bottom}} = E_{\text{bottom}} - M_{\text{bottom}}$$
     $$\text{targetScrollTop} = V.\text{scrollTop} + \Delta_{\text{bottom}} + 36\text{px}$$

4. **Case 4: Element in Content Grid (`.content-grid-6col` in Movies, Series, or Search)**:
   For 6-column grids where elements are not grouped in shelves:
   - If $E_{\text{top}} < M_{\text{top}}$:
     $$\text{targetScrollTop} = \max\left(0, V.\text{scrollTop} - (M_{\text{top}} - E_{\text{top}}) - 24\text{px}\right)$$
   - If $E_{\text{bottom}} > M_{\text{bottom}}$:
     $$\text{targetScrollTop} = V.\text{scrollTop} + (E_{\text{bottom}} - M_{\text{bottom}}) + 36\text{px}$$

5. **Case 5: Element is Already Fully Inside $[104\text{px}, 1026\text{px}]$**:
   No vertical scroll operation is performed.

#### Implementation Specification:
```javascript
SpatialNav.autoScrollViewport = function (element) {
  if (!element) return;

  // Header items do not scroll pane
  if (element.closest('.app-header')) {
    var activePane = document.querySelector('.view.active .view-scroll-pane');
    if (activePane && activePane.scrollTop !== 0) {
      activePane.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
    }
    return;
  }

  var pane = element.closest('.view-scroll-pane');
  if (!pane) return;

  var EFFECTIVE_Y_MIN = 104; // 84px header + 20px padding
  var SAFE_Y_MAX = 1026;      // 1080 - 54

  // Check if element is in Hero
  if (element.closest('.hero-banner')) {
    if (pane.scrollTop !== 0) {
      pane.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
    }
    return;
  }

  var shelf = element.closest('.content-shelf');
  var currentScrollY = pane.scrollTop;

  if (shelf) {
    var shelfRect = shelf.getBoundingClientRect();
    var cardRect = element.getBoundingClientRect();

    // 1. If shelf header is scrolled above top boundary, scroll up to reveal header
    if (shelfRect.top < EFFECTIVE_Y_MIN) {
      var deltaUp = EFFECTIVE_Y_MIN - shelfRect.top;
      var targetUp = Math.max(0, currentScrollY - deltaUp);
      pane.scrollTo({ top: targetUp, behavior: throttleState.rapidCount > 2 ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
      return;
    }

    // 2. If card bottom is clipped below bottom safe boundary, scroll down
    if (cardRect.bottom > SAFE_Y_MAX) {
      var deltaDown = cardRect.bottom - SAFE_Y_MAX;
      var targetDown = currentScrollY + deltaDown + 36;
      pane.scrollTo({ top: targetDown, behavior: throttleState.rapidCount > 2 ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
      return;
    }
    return;
  }

  // Generic grid or list item
  var itemRect = element.getBoundingClientRect();
  if (itemRect.top < EFFECTIVE_Y_MIN) {
    var diffTop = EFFECTIVE_Y_MIN - itemRect.top;
    pane.scrollTo({ top: Math.max(0, currentScrollY - diffTop - 24), behavior: throttleState.rapidCount > 2 ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
  } else if (itemRect.bottom > SAFE_Y_MAX) {
    var diffBottom = itemRect.bottom - SAFE_Y_MAX;
    pane.scrollTo({ top: currentScrollY + diffBottom + 36, behavior: throttleState.rapidCount > 2 ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
  }
};
```

