## 4. Integration Contract with CinejoyApp & Components

### 4.1 Integration Architecture with `CinejoyApp`

`SpatialNav` operates as the low-level focus and input engine, while `CinejoyApp` serves as the high-level application orchestrator. The interface boundary between them is defined by three integration touchpoints:

```
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                  CinejoyApp                                   |
|                                                                               |
|  1. init()              --->  SpatialNav.init({...callbacks...})             |
|  2. switchView(view)    --->  SpatialNav.saveFocus(current)                   |
|                               DOM switch                                      |
|                               SpatialNav.restoreFocus(newView)                |
|  3. handleBack()        <---  Invoked by SpatialNav on keycode 461 / 27       |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

#### Step 1: Bootstrap & Hook Registration in `CinejoyApp.init()`:
```javascript
// Inside CinejoyApp.init():
SpatialNav.init({
  navSelector: '[data-nav="true"]',
  activeClass: 'focused',
  tvSafeX: 96,
  tvSafeY: 54,
  headerHeight: 84,
  onBack: function () {
    return CinejoyApp.handleBackNavigation();
  },
  onSelect: function (element) {
    // Allow element.click() to process via existing delegated click listeners
  },
  onMediaKey: function (data) {
    CinejoyApp.handleMediaKey(data.action);
  },
  onColorKey: function (data) {
    CinejoyApp.handleColorKey(data.color);
  }
});
```

#### Step 2: Focus Memory Preservation in `CinejoyApp.switchView(viewName)`:
```javascript
// Inside CinejoyApp.switchView(viewName, data):
// 1. Save focus of view we are leaving
if (this.state.currentView) {
  SpatialNav.saveFocus(this.state.currentView);
}

// 2. Perform DOM view transition (hide current view, show target view)
// ...

// 3. Restore focus for incoming view
SpatialNav.restoreFocus(viewName);
```

